Subject: [PATCH] Papo: batch 147 (R7) share the canonical single-value Data
 across constant paletted containers - the re-baselined 0.84.0 soak census
 (6,059 chunks, 861.6MB) measured 394,848 LevelChunkSections of which 87% hold
 single-value block palettes, plus 232,765 single-value biome containers: 576k
 trivial containers each paying Data(32B) + SingleValuePalette(24B) + the
 moonrise$palette/rawPalette Object[1](24B) ~= 80B of state that depends only
 on (strategy, value). Each preset-free constant container now shares one
 canonical Data per (strategy, registry id) - the value is keyed by its
 registry id so the canonical instance IS the interned registry value and
 SingleValuePalette.idFor's reference comparison behaves identically. Safety
 contract, audited against every mutation path: a published shared Data is
 never structurally mutated - growth replaces the owning container's data
 field with a private Data (onResize), the only in-place palette writes are
 the reference-idempotent idFor(same value) assignments,
 Data.copy()/palette.copy() stay read-only or route through the same
 container-level swap, and the FriendlyByteBuf read() path (the one in-place
 palette rewrite, SingleValuePalette.read - server chunks load via the NBT
 codec, never this path) is guarded to allocate private data for both the
 shared Data and the shared-palette-through-copy shapes. The cache lives on
 the Strategy instance (collected with an unloaded level, bounded by registry
 size, no user-data growth); unregistered values never share. Two hooks cover
 every birth site: the generation-path public constructor
 (PalettedContainerFactory.createForBlockStates/createForBiomes) and the
 disk-decode private constructor (codec unpack) which canonicalizes
 single-value decodes (null-valued corrupt palettes keep private data).
 Coverage: PapoPalettedSharedDataTest (sharing + per-strategy isolation,
 idempotent-write keeps shared data, growth detaches without touching sharers,
 codec decode canonicalizes with byte-identical pack, copy/recreate
 independence, unregistered values never share, buffer-read forces private
 data for both guard shapes, 8-thread creation convergence)


